doc:sec-536pq-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536PQ(3) Terms that may be included in a road transport contractual" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The FWC must remove a term covered by this section that is included in a road transport contractual chain order if: (a) the FWC decides to vary the order as a result of an application for a determination varying or revoking the order that is an emergency application; and  Chapter 3B  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain" ;
    cof:pageNumber "51"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536pr a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536PR Terms that must not be included in a road transport"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536pr ;
    values:originalText "contractual chain order (1) A road transport contractual chain order must not include terms about any of the following matters: (a) overtime rates; (b) rostering arrangements; (c) a term that would change the form of the engagement or the status of a regulated road transport contractor or a road transport employee-like worker covered by the road transport contractual chain order including, but not limited to, a term that deems a regulated road transport contractor or a road transport employee-like worker to be an employee; (d) a matter relating to work health and safety that is otherwise comprehensively dealt with by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (e) a matter prescribed by the regulations, or included in a class of matter prescribed by the regulations. (2) A road transport contractual chain order must not include terms about any of the following matters: (a) a matter relating to road transport that is otherwise comprehensively dealt with: (i) by the Heavy Vehicle National Law as set out in the Schedule to the Heavy Vehicle National Law Act 2012 (Qld); or (ii) by another law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (b) a matter prescribed by the regulations, or included in a class of matter prescribed by the regulations. (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d): (a) the regulations may specify that a particular matter, or a matter included in a class of matters, is, or is not, dealt with  Chapter 3B  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain" ;
    skos:definition "contractual chain order (1) A road transport contractual chain order must not include terms about any of the following matters: (a) overtime rates; (b) rostering arrangements; (c) a term that would change the form of the engagement or the status of a regulated road transport contractor or a road transport employee-like worker covered by the road transport contractual chain order including, but not limited to, a term that deems a regulated road transport contractor or a road transport employee-like worker to be an employee; (d) a matter relating to work health and safety that is otherwise comprehensively dealt with by a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (e) a matter prescribed by the regulations, or included in a class of matter prescribed by the regulations. (2) A road transport contractual chain order must not include terms about any of the following matters: (a) a matter relating to road transport that is otherwise comprehensively dealt with: (i) by the Heavy Vehicle National Law as set out in the Schedule to the Heavy Vehicle National Law Act 2012 (Qld); or (ii) by another law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; (b) a matter prescribed by the regulations, or included in a class of matter prescribed by the regulations. (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(d): (a) the regulations may specify that a particular matter, or a matter included in a class of matters, is, or is not, dealt with  Chapter 3B  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "920dd82123a471f789e81b1747bceb357921139342ba4996b6df454c538d4c5e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536pr-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536pr-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536pr-ss-3 ;
