doc:sec-536px a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536PX Minister may make a declaration suspending a road" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "transport contractual chain order (1) If the Minister considers it is in the public interest to do so, the Minister may, by notifiable instrument, make a declaration (a suspension declaration): (a) suspending the operation of a road transport contractual chain order; or (b) suspending the application of:  Chapter 3B  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536py a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536PY Suspension declaration must generally be made within 12"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536py ;
    values:originalText "months of certain dates Full suspension declaration timing (1) A full suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on the day on which the road transport contractual chain order came into operation. Part suspension declaration timing (2) A part suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on whichever of the following days is applicable: (a) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to the specified class of persons; (b) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to at least one of the specified classes of persons (even if all of the terms of the order did not apply to all of the specified classes on that day); (c) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which the specified terms first applied to the specified class of persons;  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Chapter 3B Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Part 3B-2 Deferral and suspension of road transport contractual chain orders  Division 3 Section 536PZ Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (d) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which the specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to at least one of the specified classes of persons (even if the order did not apply to all of the specified classes on that day); (e) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to all persons—the day on which the specified terms first applied to all persons. (3) The relevant period for a road transport contractual chain order is: (a) 12 months, unless paragraph (b) applies; and (b) for a time-sensitive road transport contractual chain order—3 months." ;
    skos:definition "months of certain dates Full suspension declaration timing (1) A full suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on the day on which the road transport contractual chain order came into operation. Part suspension declaration timing (2) A part suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on whichever of the following days is applicable: (a) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to the specified class of persons; (b) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to at least one of the specified classes of persons (even if all of the terms of the order did not apply to all of the specified classes on that day); (c) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which the specified terms first applied to the specified class of persons;  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Chapter 3B Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Part 3B-2 Deferral and suspension of road transport contractual chain orders  Division 3 Section 536PZ Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (d) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which the specified terms of the road transport contract"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c2c2039de89f856fb1ee3f484984fdf87291a0f7dfca9fa324dc129d1c6f0950" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536py-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536py-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536py-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.62" .
doc:sec-536py a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536PY Suspension declaration must generally be made within 12" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "months of certain dates Full suspension declaration timing (1) A full suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on the day on which the road transport contractual chain order came into operation. Part suspension declaration timing (2) A part suspension declaration in relation to a road transport contractual chain order must be made within the relevant period starting on whichever of the following days is applicable: (a) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to the specified class of persons; (b) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which all of the terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to at least one of the specified classes of persons (even if all of the terms of the order did not apply to all of the specified classes on that day); (c) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to a specified class of persons—the day on which the specified terms first applied to the specified class of persons;  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Chapter 3B Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Part 3B-2 Deferral and suspension of road transport contractual chain orders  Division 3 Section 536PZ Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (d) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to 2 or more specified classes of persons—the day on which the specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order first applied to at least one of the specified classes of persons (even if the order did not apply to all of the specified classes on that day); (e) if the part suspension declaration suspends the application of specified terms of the road transport contractual chain order to all persons—the day on which the specified terms first applied to all persons. (3) The relevant period for a road transport contractual chain order is: (a) 12 months, unless paragraph (b) applies; and (b) for a time-sensitive road transport contractual chain order—3 months." ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

