doc:sec-536qm-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "536QM(6) Affected entities to have a reasonable opportunity to make" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) For the purposes of subsection (1), an affected entity, in relation to a proposed variation or revocation of a road transport contractual chain order in relation to which a notice of intent has been published under paragraph 536QL(1)(a), is: (a) a person or body likely to be affected by the proposed variation or revocation; or (b) a person or body prescribed by the regulations, or belonging to a class of persons or bodies prescribed by the regulations.  Chapter 3B  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain" ;
    cof:pageNumber "76"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536qn a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "536QN Finalising draft order"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-536qn ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC may make any changes it thinks appropriate to a draft road transport contractual chain order as proposed to be varied. (2) If changes proposed to be made under subsection (1) are significant, the FWC must: (a) decide not to vary the road transport contractual chain order based on the draft; and (b) publish a subsequent notice of intent under paragraph 536QL(1)(a) in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order, and publish the revised draft; and (c) follow the process set out in section 536QM (as affected by subsection (3) or (4) of this section) in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order. (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), the period of consultation under section 536QM in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order is to be the period of at least 12 months starting when the subsequent notice of intent and the revised draft required by paragraph (2)(b) of this section were published. (4) However, the FWC may reduce that 12-month period to another period that the FWC considers is reasonable if the order is a time-sensitive road transport contractual chain order.  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Chapter 3B Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Part 3B-2 Road transport contractual chain guidelines  Division 5 Section 536QP Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC may make any changes it thinks appropriate to a draft road transport contractual chain order as proposed to be varied. (2) If changes proposed to be made under subsection (1) are significant, the FWC must: (a) decide not to vary the road transport contractual chain order based on the draft; and (b) publish a subsequent notice of intent under paragraph 536QL(1)(a) in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order, and publish the revised draft; and (c) follow the process set out in section 536QM (as affected by subsection (3) or (4) of this section) in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order. (3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(c), the period of consultation under section 536QM in relation to the revised draft road transport contractual chain order is to be the period of at least 12 months starting when the subsequent notice of intent and the revised draft required by paragraph (2)(b) of this section were published. (4) However, the FWC may reduce that 12-month period to another period that the FWC considers is reasonable if the order is a time-sensitive road transport contractual chain order.  Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Chapter 3B Minimum standards for persons in a road transport contractual chain  Part 3B-2 Road transport contractual chain guidelines  Division 5 Section 536QP Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5666defe325b1966185f4bdeffefb0931c3b34d4dfb8329d3fbc6e34f3ddf9c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536qn-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536qn-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536qn-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-536qn-ss-4 ;
