doc:sec-545-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "545(1) Orders that can be made by particular courts" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) may make any order the court considers appropriate if the court is satisfied that a person has contravened, or proposes to contravene, a civil remedy provision. Note 1: For the court’s power to make pecuniary penalty orders, see section 546. Note 2: For limitations on orders in relation to costs, see section 570. Note 3: The Federal Court and the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) may grant injunctions in relation to industrial action under subsections 417(3) and 421(3).  Compliance and enforcement  Chapter 4 Civil remedies  Part 4-1 Orders  Division 2 Section 545 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Note 4: There are limitations on orders that can be made in relation to contraventions of subsection 463(1) or (2) (which deals with protected action ballot orders) (see subsection 463(3))." ;
    cof:pageNumber "124"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-545-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "545(2) Orders that can be made by particular courts"@en ;
