concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-545-ss-3a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "545(3A) Orders that can be made by particular courts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-545-ss-3a ;
    values:originalText "(3A) An eligible State or Territory court may order an outworker entity to pay an amount to, or on behalf of, an outworker if the court is satisfied that: (a) the outworker entity was required to pay the amount under a modern award; and (b) the outworker entity has contravened a civil remedy provision by failing to pay the amount. Note 1: For the court’s power to make pecuniary penalty orders, see section 546.  Chapter 4  Compliance and enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "(3A) An eligible State or Territory court may order an outworker entity to pay an amount to, or on behalf of, an outworker if the court is satisfied that: (a) the outworker entity was required to pay the amount under a modern award; and (b) the outworker entity has contravened a civil remedy provision by failing to pay the amount. Note 1: For the court’s power to make pecuniary penalty orders, see section 546.  Chapter 4  Compliance and enforcement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "50ff82ccd78d5d4ed27b58aff93a092c3d9e2e09871c63161de6f8ab79aaa6b8" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-545 ;
