doc:sec-558b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "558B Responsibility of responsible franchisor entities and holding" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "companies for certain contraventions Responsible franchisor entities (1) A person contravenes this subsection if: (a) an employer who is a franchisee entity of a franchise contravenes a civil remedy provision referred to in subsection (7); and (b) the person is a responsible franchisor entity for the franchisee entity; and (c) the contravention by the franchisee entity occurs in the franchisee entity’s capacity as a franchisee entity; and (d) either:  Chapter 4  Compliance and enforcement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "145"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-558c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "558C Right of responsible franchisor entity or holding company to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-558c ;
    values:originalText "recover (1) This section applies if: (a) a person pays an amount to, or on behalf of, an employee pursuant to an order under subsection 545(1) relating to a contravention by the person of subsection 558B(1) or (2) in relation to a franchisee entity or subsidiary (the contravening employer); and (b) the person has not otherwise recovered from the contravening employer an amount (the recoverable amount) equal to the amount paid by the person. (2) The person may commence proceedings against the contravening employer for payment to the person of so much of the recoverable amount as has not been recovered. (3) The proceedings may be commenced in: (a) the Federal Court; or (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or  Chapter 4  Compliance and enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "recover (1) This section applies if: (a) a person pays an amount to, or on behalf of, an employee pursuant to an order under subsection 545(1) relating to a contravention by the person of subsection 558B(1) or (2) in relation to a franchisee entity or subsidiary (the contravening employer); and (b) the person has not otherwise recovered from the contravening employer an amount (the recoverable amount) equal to the amount paid by the person. (2) The person may commence proceedings against the contravening employer for payment to the person of so much of the recoverable amount as has not been recovered. (3) The proceedings may be commenced in: (a) the Federal Court; or (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or  Chapter 4  Compliance and enforcement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ec3915f542e0f8cb6c1832fbb0389a011fe48b6a82e37f7940e274bf23020776" ;
    cof:pageNumber "149"^^xsd:integer ;
