doc:sec-563 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "563 Exercising jurisdiction in the Fair Work Division of the Federal" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Court The jurisdiction conferred on the Federal Court under section 562 is to be exercised in the Fair Work Division of the Federal Court if: (a) an application is made to the Federal Court under this Act; or (b) a writ of mandamus or prohibition or an injunction is sought in the Federal Court against a person holding office under this Act; or (c) a declaration is sought under section 21 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 in relation to a matter arising under this Act; or (d) an injunction is sought under section 23 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 in relation to a matter arising under this Act; or (e) a prosecution is instituted in the Federal Court under this Act; or (f) an appeal is instituted in the Federal Court from a judgment of the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) or a court of a State or Territory in a matter arising under this Act; or (g) proceedings in relation to a matter arising under this Act are transferred to the Federal Court from the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or (h) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) or a court of a State or Territory states a case or reserves a question for the consideration of the Federal Court in a matter arising under this Act; or  Compliance and enforcement  Chapter 4 Jurisdiction and powers of courts  Part 4-2 Jurisdiction and powers of the Federal Court  Division 2 Section 564 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (i) the President refers, under section 608 of this Act, a question of law to the Federal Court; or (j) the High Court remits a matter arising under this Act to the Federal Court." ;
    cof:pageNumber "154"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-564 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "564 No limitation on Federal Court’s powers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-564 ;
    values:originalText "To avoid doubt, nothing in this Act limits the Federal Court’s powers under section 21, 22 or 23 of the Federal Court of Australia Act 1976." ;
