concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-569 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "569 Minister’s entitlement to intervene"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-569 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may intervene on behalf of the Commonwealth in proceedings before a court (including a court of a State or Territory) in relation to a matter arising under this Act if the Minister believes it is in the public interest to do so. (2) If the Minister intervenes, the Minister is taken to be a party to the proceedings for the purposes of instituting an appeal from a judgment given in the proceedings. (3) Despite section 570, a court may make an order as to costs against the Commonwealth if: (a) the Minister intervenes under subsection (1); or (b) the Minister institutes an appeal from a judgment as referred to in subsection (2)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may intervene on behalf of the Commonwealth in proceedings before a court (including a court of a State or Territory) in relation to a matter arising under this Act if the Minister believes it is in the public interest to do so. (2) If the Minister intervenes, the Minister is taken to be a party to the proceedings for the purposes of instituting an appeal from a judgment given in the proceedings. (3) Despite section 570, a court may make an order as to costs against the Commonwealth if: (a) the Minister intervenes under subsection (1); or (b) the Minister institutes an appeal from a judgment as referred to in subsection (2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c45b1d7cdb733a188659484ca35a0fc513d4cb2773c72a510fd026d7dcb1d056" ;
    cof:pageNumber "159"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-569-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-569-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-569-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
