concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-597 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "597 Minister’s entitlement to make submissions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-597 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister is entitled to make a submission for consideration in relation to a matter before the FWC if: (a) the matter is before a Full Bench and it is in the public interest for the Minister to make a submission; or (b) the matter involves public sector employment. (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the FWC holds a hearing in relation to the matter." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister is entitled to make a submission for consideration in relation to a matter before the FWC if: (a) the matter is before a Full Bench and it is in the public interest for the Minister to make a submission; or (b) the matter involves public sector employment. (2) Subsection (1) applies whether or not the FWC holds a hearing in relation to the matter."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4940497f35d5f4a0def2a81db39450d9f9d15b7bcfc3a765de07db3055b08c65" ;
    cof:pageNumber "179"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-597-ss-1 ;
