doc:sec-608-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "608(4) Referring questions of law to the Federal Court" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Once the Federal Court has determined the question, the FWC may only make a decision in relation to the matter that is not inconsistent with the opinion of the Federal Court (if the FWC has not already done so)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-608-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "608(5) Referring questions of law to the Federal Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-608-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) However, if the FWC has made a decision in relation to the matter that is inconsistent with the opinion of the Federal Court, the FWC must vary the decision in such a way as to make it consistent with the opinion of the Federal Court. Subdivision F—Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(5) However, if the FWC has made a decision in relation to the matter that is inconsistent with the opinion of the Federal Court, the FWC must vary the decision in such a way as to make it consistent with the opinion of the Federal Court. Subdivision F—Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4069db99a5eb9dee28ace5cacc30d572705165af9ebd152fe7a842bf0888cce8" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-608 ;
    cof:pageNumber "188"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must vary decision to make it consistent with Federal Court's opinion." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
