concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-613 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "613 Appeal of decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-613 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A Full Bench must (except as provided by subsection (2)): (a) decide under section 604 whether to grant permission to appeal a decision; and (b) if the Full Bench decides to grant the permission—hear the appeal in accordance with section 607. Note: For the constitution of a Full Bench, see section 618. (2) The President, a Vice President or a Deputy President directed by the President, may: (a) decide under section 604 whether to grant permission to appeal: (i) a decision of a delegate under subsection 625(2); or  Chapter 5  Administration" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A Full Bench must (except as provided by subsection (2)): (a) decide under section 604 whether to grant permission to appeal a decision; and (b) if the Full Bench decides to grant the permission—hear the appeal in accordance with section 607. Note: For the constitution of a Full Bench, see section 618. (2) The President, a Vice President or a Deputy President directed by the President, may: (a) decide under section 604 whether to grant permission to appeal: (i) a decision of a delegate under subsection 625(2); or  Chapter 5  Administration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e328344db702350810fea8ee21d7a5fb7acd319641e869f2af8e906072d06830" ;
    cof:pageNumber "191"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-613-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-613-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.191" .
