concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-617a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "617A President may direct investigations and reports"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-617a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The President may give a direction under section 582 requiring that a matter that is relevant to the function of an Expert Panel constituted under subsection 620(1B), (1C), (1D) or (1E) be investigated, and that a report about the matter be prepared. Note: Matters that may be relevant include gender pay equity, equal remuneration, the road transport industry, and the Care and Community Sector, in Australia. (2) The direction may be given to: (a) an Expert Panel; or (b) an Expert Panel Member; or (c) a Commissioner; or (d) a Full Bench that includes one or more Expert Panel Members.  Chapter 5  Administration" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The President may give a direction under section 582 requiring that a matter that is relevant to the function of an Expert Panel constituted under subsection 620(1B), (1C), (1D) or (1E) be investigated, and that a report about the matter be prepared. Note: Matters that may be relevant include gender pay equity, equal remuneration, the road transport industry, and the Care and Community Sector, in Australia. (2) The direction may be given to: (a) an Expert Panel; or (b) an Expert Panel Member; or (c) a Commissioner; or (d) a Full Bench that includes one or more Expert Panel Members.  Chapter 5  Administration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "30e3254cc73475afe9bbd824be1b543cdbf3d5efd1dad3331020453bf29f7ed7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "203"^^xsd:integer ;
