concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-619 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "619 Seniority of FWC Members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-619 ;
    values:originalText "(1) While the FWC is constituted by a Full Bench, the FWC Members on the Full Bench have seniority according to the following order: (a) the President;  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 Organisation of the FWC  Division 4 Section 620 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (aa) the Vice Presidents, according to the days on which their appointments as Vice Presidents took effect; (ab) if 2 appointments as Vice Presidents took effect on the same day—the Vice Presidents, according to the precedence assigned to them in their instruments of appointment; (b) the Deputy Presidents, according to the days on which their appointments as Deputy Presidents took effect; (c) if 2 or more appointments as Deputy Presidents took effect on the same day—the Deputy Presidents, according to the precedence assigned to them in their instruments of appointment. (2) The FWC Member on a Full Bench who has seniority under this section is responsible for managing the Full Bench in performing functions and exercising powers of the FWC. Note: The FWC Member who has seniority also has a deciding vote if there is no majority (see subsection 618(4))." ;
    skos:definition "(1) While the FWC is constituted by a Full Bench, the FWC Members on the Full Bench have seniority according to the following order: (a) the President;  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 Organisation of the FWC  Division 4 Section 620 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (aa) the Vice Presidents, according to the days on which their appointments as Vice Presidents took effect; (ab) if 2 appointments as Vice Presidents took effect on the same day—the Vice Presidents, according to the precedence assigned to them in their instruments of appointment; (b) the Deputy Presidents, according to the days on which their appointments as Deputy Presidents took effect; (c) if 2 or more appointments as Deputy Presidents took effect on the same day—the Deputy Presidents, according to the precedence assigned to them in their instruments of appointment. (2) The FWC Member on a Full Bench who has seniority under this section is responsible for managing the Full Bench in performing functions and exercising powers of the FWC. Note: The FWC Member who has seniority also has a deciding vote if there is no majority (see subsection 618(4))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8001427c92fb542fce8ecff8ec1126086a5622e689ed2055cf410eca15c96901" ;
    cof:pageNumber "204"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-619-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-619-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
