    values:borneBy values:Agent ;
    values:deonticStatus values:HeuristicDerived ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-632 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "632 Dual federal and Territory appointments of Deputy Presidents" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "or Commissioners Nothing in this Act prevents a Deputy President or Commissioner from being appointed to, and holding at the same time, one of the following offices, with the President’s approval: (a) an office as a member of a Commonwealth or Territory tribunal prescribed by the regulations (other than a court); (b) an office under a Commonwealth or Territory law." ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-633 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "633 Outside work of FWC Members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-633 ;
    values:originalText "Vice Presidents, Deputy Presidents and Commissioners (1) A Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner (whether performing duties on a full-time or part-time basis) must not engage in paid work outside the duties of his or her office without the President’s approval. (2) However, the President’s approval is not required if the paid work is an office or appointment in the Defence Force. Expert Panel Members (3) An Expert Panel Member must not engage in any paid work that, in the President’s opinion, conflicts or may conflict with the proper performance of his or her duties." ;
    skos:definition "Vice Presidents, Deputy Presidents and Commissioners (1) A Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner (whether performing duties on a full-time or part-time basis) must not engage in paid work outside the duties of his or her office without the President’s approval. (2) However, the President’s approval is not required if the paid work is an office or appointment in the Defence Force. Expert Panel Members (3) An Expert Panel Member must not engage in any paid work that, in the President’s opinion, conflicts or may conflict with the proper performance of his or her duties."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "096fa0f99e35d6e4ff127016a61e04dbc95f5767cd6228fd109c237f3e42577a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-633-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-633-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-633-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
