doc:sec-640-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "640(2) Disclosure of interests by FWC Members other than the" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) The FWC Member must disclose the potential conflict to:  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 FWC Members  Division 5 Section 641 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 (a) a person who has made, or will make, a submission for consideration in the matter; and (b) a person who the FWC Member considers is likely to make a submission for consideration in the matter; and (c) the President." ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-640-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "640(4) Disclosure of interests by FWC Members other than the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-640-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The President must give a direction to the FWC Member not to deal, or to no longer deal, with the matter if: (a) the President becomes aware that an FWC Member has a potential conflict in relation to a matter (whether or not because of a disclosure under subsection (2)); and (b) the President considers that the FWC Member should not deal, or should no longer deal, with the matter." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The President must give a direction to the FWC Member not to deal, or to no longer deal, with the matter if: (a) the President becomes aware that an FWC Member has a potential conflict in relation to a matter (whether or not because of a disclosure under subsection (2)); and (b) the President considers that the FWC Member should not deal, or should no longer deal, with the matter."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6e3d674cb9ecbdf46c45f02acb89b5dcfcf1296f544fd9aa3ce4dae3086edcda" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-640 ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Prohibit FWC Member from dealing with matter if President considers conflict of interest." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
