concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-644 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "644 Termination of appointment for outside work"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-644 ;
    values:originalText "Vice Presidents, Deputy Presidents and Commissioners (1) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner if the Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner engages, except with the  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 FWC Members  Division 5 Section 645 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 President’s approval, in paid work outside the duties of his or her office (see subsection 633(1)). Expert Panel Members (2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of an Expert Panel Member if the Expert Panel Member engages in paid work that, in the President’s opinion, conflicts or may conflict with the proper performance of his or her duties (see subsection 633(3))." ;
    skos:definition "Vice Presidents, Deputy Presidents and Commissioners (1) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner if the Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner engages, except with the  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 FWC Members  Division 5 Section 645 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 President’s approval, in paid work outside the duties of his or her office (see subsection 633(1)). Expert Panel Members (2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of an Expert Panel Member if the Expert Panel Member engages in paid work that, in the President’s opinion, conflicts or may conflict with the proper performance of his or her duties (see subsection 633(3))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "096fa0f99e35d6e4ff127016a61e04dbc95f5767cd6228fd109c237f3e42577a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-644-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-644-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.232" .
doc:sec-644 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "644 Termination of appointment for outside work" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Vice Presidents, Deputy Presidents and Commissioners (1) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of a Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner if the Vice President, Deputy President or Commissioner engages, except with the  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 FWC Members  Division 5 Section 645 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 President’s approval, in paid work outside the duties of his or her office (see subsection 633(1)). Expert Panel Members (2) The Governor-General must terminate the appointment of an Expert Panel Member if the Expert Panel Member engages in paid work that, in the President’s opinion, conflicts or may conflict with the proper performance of his or her duties (see subsection 633(3))." ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer .

