concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-660 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "660 Appointment of the General Manager"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-660 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The General Manager is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument on the nomination of the President. (2) The General Manager holds office on a full-time basis. (3) The General Manager holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years. Note: The General Manager is eligible for reappointment (see subsection 33(4A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The General Manager is to be appointed by the Governor-General by written instrument on the nomination of the President. (2) The General Manager holds office on a full-time basis. (3) The General Manager holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 5 years. Note: The General Manager is eligible for reappointment (see subsection 33(4A) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901)."@en ;
