doc:sec-676 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "676 Intimidation etc." ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A person commits an offence if: (a) the person threatens, intimidates, coerces or prejudices another person; and (b) the person does so because the other person has given, or proposes to give, information or documents to the FWC. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months. Note: A person may also contravene a civil remedy provision by threatening etc. a person who has given, or proposes to give, information or documents to the FWC (see section 343).  Administration  Chapter 5 The Fair Work Commission  Part 5-1 Offences relating to the Fair Work Commission  Division 9 Section 677 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-677 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "677 Offences in relation to attending before the FWC"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-677 ;
    values:originalText "Required to attend (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person has been required to attend before the FWC; and (b) the person fails to attend as required. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Oath or affirmation (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person attends before the FWC; and (b) the FWC requires the person to take an oath or make an affirmation; and (c) the person refuses or fails to be sworn or to make an affirmation as required. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Questions or documents (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person attends before the FWC; and (b) the FWC requires the person to answer a question or produce a document; and (c) the person refuses or fails to answer the question or produce the document. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Reasonable excuse (4) Subsection (1), (2) or (3) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  Chapter 5  Administration" ;
    skos:definition "Required to attend (1) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person has been required to attend before the FWC; and (b) the person fails to attend as required. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Oath or affirmation (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person attends before the FWC; and (b) the FWC requires the person to take an oath or make an affirmation; and (c) the person refuses or fails to be sworn or to make an affirmation as required. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Questions or documents (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person attends before the FWC; and (b) the FWC requires the person to answer a question or produce a document; and (c) the person refuses or fails to answer the question or produce the document. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months. Reasonable excuse (4) Subsection (1), (2) or (3) does not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (4) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  Chapter 5  Administration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3febd3fbac8ce40b07f79465356b0c2e8e510378d2805c02bd19d9fca682ffbc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "253"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-677-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-677-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-677-ss-3 ;
