    cof:pageNumber "268"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-708 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "708 Power of inspectors to enter premises"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-708 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An inspector may, without force: (a) enter premises, if the inspector reasonably believes that this Act or a fair work instrument applies to work that is being, or applied to work that has been, performed on the premises; or (b) enter business premises, if the inspector reasonably believes that there are records or documents relevant to compliance purposes on the premises, or accessible from a computer on the premises. (2) Despite paragraph (1)(a), an inspector must not enter a part of premises that is used for residential purposes unless the inspector reasonably believes that the work referred to in that paragraph is being performed on that part of the premises. (3) The inspector must, either before or as soon as practicable after entering premises, show his or her identity card to the occupier, or another person who apparently represents the occupier, if the occupier or other person is present at the premises." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An inspector may, without force: (a) enter premises, if the inspector reasonably believes that this Act or a fair work instrument applies to work that is being, or applied to work that has been, performed on the premises; or (b) enter business premises, if the inspector reasonably believes that there are records or documents relevant to compliance purposes on the premises, or accessible from a computer on the premises. (2) Despite paragraph (1)(a), an inspector must not enter a part of premises that is used for residential purposes unless the inspector reasonably believes that the work referred to in that paragraph is being performed on that part of the premises. (3) The inspector must, either before or as soon as practicable after entering premises, show his or her identity card to the occupier, or another person who apparently represents the occupier, if the occupier or other person is present at the premises."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cb2c1b1f6ee439d0710cee932413719dd1f69edd0b2b30fe75f0c033f447293c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "269"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-708-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-708-ss-2 ;
