    values:originalText "(1) A person must not give information or produce a document to the Fair Work Ombudsman, an inspector, or a person referred to in subsection 712AA(2), (the official) exercising powers or performing functions under, or in connection with, a law of the Commonwealth if the person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the information or the document: (a) is false or misleading; or (b) for information—omits any matter or thing without which the information is misleading. Note 1: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1).  Administration  Chapter 5 Office of the Fair Work Ombudsman  Part 5-2 Office of the Fair Work Ombudsman  Division 3 Section 718A Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026 Note 2: Sections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for providing false or misleading information or documents." ;
