doc:sec-736 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "736 Meanings of employee and employer" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In this Part, employee means a national system employee, and employer means a national system employer. Note: See also Division 2 of Part 6-4A (TCF contract outworkers taken to be employees in certain circumstances).  Miscellaneous  Chapter 6 Dealing with disputes  Part 6-2 Dealing with disputes  Division 2 Section 737 Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "310"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-737 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "737 Model term about dealing with disputes"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-737 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The FWC must determine a model term for dealing with disputes for enterprise agreements. (2) In determining the model term, the FWC must: (a) ensure that the model term is consistent with the requirements set out in subsection 186(6); and (b) take into account the following matters: (i) whether the model term is broadly consistent with comparable terms in modern awards; (ii) best practice workplace relations as determined by the FWC; (iii) whether all persons and bodies have had a reasonable opportunity to be heard and make submissions to the FWC for consideration in determining the model term; (iv) the operation of subsections 739(3), (4), (5) and (6) and 740(3) and (4); (v) the object of this Act (see section 3); (vi) any other matters the FWC considers relevant. Note 1: The FWC must be constituted by a Full Bench to make the model term dealing with disputes (see subsection 616(4A)). Note 2: For the variation of a determination, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (3) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument, but section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The FWC must determine a model term for dealing with disputes for enterprise agreements. (2) In determining the model term, the FWC must: (a) ensure that the model term is consistent with the requirements set out in subsection 186(6); and (b) take into account the following matters: (i) whether the model term is broadly consistent with comparable terms in modern awards; (ii) best practice workplace relations as determined by the FWC; (iii) whether all persons and bodies have had a reasonable opportunity to be heard and make submissions to the FWC for consideration in determining the model term; (iv) the operation of subsections 739(3), (4), (5) and (6) and 740(3) and (4); (v) the object of this Act (see section 3); (vi) any other matters the FWC considers relevant. Note 1: The FWC must be constituted by a Full Bench to make the model term dealing with disputes (see subsection 616(4A)). Note 2: For the variation of a determination, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (3) A determination under subsection (1) is a legislative instrument, but section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the determination.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "646075f076712a5b3a22f07c21e984b09177cfc2d7fde20c5e67182df255a61f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "311"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-737-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-737-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-737-ss-3 ;
