doc:sec-768ar-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "768AR(2) Provisions of the NES that allow instruments to contain" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a copied State instrument for a transferring employee: (a) includes terms referred to in subsection 93(1) but the terms do not include the requirements referred to in subsection 93(2); or (b) includes terms referred to in subsection 101(1) but the terms do not include the requirements referred to in subsection 101(2); then the instrument is taken to include terms that include the requirements. Shiftworker annual leave entitlement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "344"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768ar-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "768AR(3) Provisions of the NES that allow instruments to contain"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-768ar-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If a copied State instrument for a transferring employee applies to the employee, then subsections 87(3) to (5) have effect, on and after the employee’s re-employment time, in the same way as they apply to an award/agreement free employee. Note: If the transferring employee qualifies for the shiftworker annual leave entitlement under those subsections, the employee will be entitled to 5 (rather than 4) weeks of paid annual leave.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If a copied State instrument for a transferring employee applies to the employee, then subsections 87(3) to (5) have effect, on and after the employee’s re-employment time, in the same way as they apply to an award/agreement free employee. Note: If the transferring employee qualifies for the shiftworker annual leave entitlement under those subsections, the employee will be entitled to 5 (rather than 4) weeks of paid annual leave.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8aebe1c235bf8a7a7451cf7b615269ce4290c2ae794ae617d5198cdaca48c1ac" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768ar ;
    cof:pageNumber "344"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "If a copied State instrument applies to the employee, subsections 87(3) to (5) have effect." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.344" ;
