concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768br a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "768BR Cessation not intended to result in reduction in take-home"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-768br ;
    values:originalText "pay (1) If a copied State award for a transferring employee ceases to operate because of subsection 768AO(2), the cessation is not intended to result in a reduction in the take-home pay of the employee. (2) A transferring employee’s take-home pay is the pay the employee actually receives: (a) including wages and incentive-based payments, and additional amounts such as allowances and overtime; but (b) disregarding the effect of any deductions that are made as permitted by section 324. Note: Deductions permitted by section 324 may (for example) include deductions under salary sacrificing arrangements. (3) A transferring employee suffers a reduction in take-home pay if, and only if: (a) when the copied State award for the employee ceases to operate because of subsection 768AO(2), the employee becomes a person to whom a modern award applies; and (b) the employee is employed in the same position as (or a position that is comparable to) the position he or she was employed in immediately before the cessation of the copied State award; and (c) the amount of the employee’s take-home pay for working particular hours or for a particular quantity of work after the cessation of the copied State award is less than what would have been the employee’s take-home pay for those hours or that quantity of work immediately before the cessation; and (d) that reduction in the employee’s take-home pay is attributable to the cessation of the copied State award.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 6 Transfer of business from a State public sector employer  Part 6-3A Special rules for copied State instruments  Division 8 Section 768BS Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026" ;
    skos:definition "pay (1) If a copied State award for a transferring employee ceases to operate because of subsection 768AO(2), the cessation is not intended to result in a reduction in the take-home pay of the employee. (2) A transferring employee’s take-home pay is the pay the employee actually receives: (a) including wages and incentive-based payments, and additional amounts such as allowances and overtime; but (b) disregarding the effect of any deductions that are made as permitted by section 324. Note: Deductions permitted by section 324 may (for example) include deductions under salary sacrificing arrangements. (3) A transferring employee suffers a reduction in take-home pay if, and only if: (a) when the copied State award for the employee ceases to operate because of subsection 768AO(2), the employee becomes a person to whom a modern award applies; and (b) the employee is employed in the same position as (or a position that is comparable to) the position he or she was employed in immediately before the cessation of the copied State award; and (c) the amount of the employee’s take-home pay for working particular hours or for a particular quantity of work after the cessation of the copied State award is less than what would have been the employee’s take-home pay for those hours or that quantity of work immediately before the cessation; and (d) that reduction in the employee’s take-home pay is attributable to the cessation of the copied State award.  Miscellaneous  Chapter 6 Transfer of business from a State public sector employer  Part 6-3A Special rules for copied State instruments  Division 8 Section 768BS Fair Work Act 2009 Compilation date: 02/04/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9350872d712a127c494d7dc35e46b0bc9e62e288239708e581dfc3a1400154a4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "372"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768br-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768br-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-768br-ss-3 ;
