 (i) in good faith; and (ii) to avoid injury to the religious susceptibilities of adherents of that religion or creed. (3) To avoid doubt, if: (a) an employer terminates an employee’s employment; and (b) the reason, or a reason, for the termination is that the position held by the employee no longer exists, or will no longer exist; and (c) the reason, or a reason, that the position held by the employee no longer exists, or will no longer exist, is the employee’s absence, or proposed or probable absence, during parental leave; the employee’s employment is taken, for the purposes of paragraph (1)(g), to have been terminated for the reason, or for reasons including the reason, of absence from work during parental leave. (4) For the purposes of subsection (1), subsection 109(2) (which deals with the meaning of voluntary emergency management activity) has effect as if the word employee had its ordinary meaning." ;
