doc:sec-785-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "785(4) Employer to notify Centrelink of certain proposed terminations" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The employer must not terminate an employee’s employment in accordance with the decision unless the employer has complied with this section. Note: This subsection is a civil remedy provision (see Part 4-1)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-785-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "785(5) Employer to notify Centrelink of certain proposed terminations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-785-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) The orders that may be made under subsection 545(1) in relation to a contravention of subsection (4) of this section: (a) include an order requiring the employer not to terminate the employment of employees in accordance with the decision, except as permitted by the order; but (b) do not include an order granting an injunction. Subdivision C—Failure to notify or consult registered employee associations" ;
    skos:definition "(5) The orders that may be made under subsection 545(1) in relation to a contravention of subsection (4) of this section: (a) include an order requiring the employer not to terminate the employment of employees in accordance with the decision, except as permitted by the order; but (b) do not include an order granting an injunction. Subdivision C—Failure to notify or consult registered employee associations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "620cf0dcff15a8a829aadba38dd53dcb338e1138f12bf5edb2be4520a728eca5" ;
    values:partOf concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-785 ;
    cof:pageNumber "394"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Employer must not terminate employment without Centrelink's permission." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
