concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789cd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "789CD Court order for entity to pay amount demanded"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-789cd ;
    values:originalText "(1) If: (a) in accordance with section 789CC, an apparent indirectly responsible entity has been given a demand for payment of a specified amount; and (b) the amount has not been paid in full by the time specified in the demand; a person or organisation specified in subsection (2) (the applicant) may commence proceedings for an order requiring the entity to pay the specified amount. (2) The proceedings may be commenced: (a) by the TCF outworker; or (b) on the TCF outworker’s behalf, by: (i) an organisation that is entitled to represent the industrial interests of the outworker; or (ii) an inspector. (3) The proceedings may be commenced in: (a) the Federal Court; or (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or (c) an eligible State or Territory court. (4) Subject only to subsections (5) and (6), the court may make an order requiring the entity to pay, to the outworker or to another person on the outworker’s behalf, the specified amount (or so much of that amount as the applicant alleges is still owing). (5) The court must not make an order under subsection (4) if the entity satisfies the court that the entity is not liable under section 789CB to pay any of the specified amount.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If: (a) in accordance with section 789CC, an apparent indirectly responsible entity has been given a demand for payment of a specified amount; and (b) the amount has not been paid in full by the time specified in the demand; a person or organisation specified in subsection (2) (the applicant) may commence proceedings for an order requiring the entity to pay the specified amount. (2) The proceedings may be commenced: (a) by the TCF outworker; or (b) on the TCF outworker’s behalf, by: (i) an organisation that is entitled to represent the industrial interests of the outworker; or (ii) an inspector. (3) The proceedings may be commenced in: (a) the Federal Court; or (b) the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2); or (c) an eligible State or Territory court. (4) Subject only to subsections (5) and (6), the court may make an order requiring the entity to pay, to the outworker or to another person on the outworker’s behalf, the specified amount (or so much of that amount as the applicant alleges is still owing). (5) The court must not make an order under subsection (4) if the entity satisfies the court that the entity is not liable under section 789CB to pay any of the specified amount.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "41ec09a38bef80cbff8d97c4362dfec0eea7289327b6518bba1f690d2d32aef5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "407"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789cd-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789cd-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789cd-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789cd-ss-4 ;
