    values:originalText "(3) The FWC may deal with a dispute only on application by any of the following: (a) an employee; (b) an employer; (c) an employee organisation; (d) an employer organisation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "430"^^xsd:integer .

concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-789gv-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "789GV(4) FWC may deal with a dispute about the operation of this"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-789gv-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The FWC may make any of the following orders: (a) an order that the FWC considers desirable to give effect to a jobkeeper enabling direction; (b) an order setting aside a jobkeeper enabling direction; (c) an order: (i) setting aside a jobkeeper enabling direction; and (ii) substituting a different jobkeeper enabling direction; (d) any other order that the FWC considers appropriate." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The FWC may make any of the following orders: (a) an order that the FWC considers desirable to give effect to a jobkeeper enabling direction; (b) an order setting aside a jobkeeper enabling direction; (c) an order: (i) setting aside a jobkeeper enabling direction; and (ii) substituting a different jobkeeper enabling direction; (d) any other order that the FWC considers appropriate."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea04943c55cf064c367e035e8d1a8c4024a8ff4e12420277d975c3abfac14458" ;
