concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-792 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "792 Delegation by Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-792 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate all or any of his or her functions or powers under this Act (except under section 32A) to: (a) the Secretary of the Department; or (b) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Department. (2) In performing functions or exercising powers under a delegation, the delegate must comply with any directions of the Minister. Note: See also sections 34AA and 34AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, in writing, delegate all or any of his or her functions or powers under this Act (except under section 32A) to: (a) the Secretary of the Department; or (b) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Department. (2) In performing functions or exercising powers under a delegation, the delegate must comply with any directions of the Minister. Note: See also sections 34AA and 34AB of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "620b11552494e0171d477395abf60b7cbaae4840cb719b10164aaeb4e3cf44a6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "448"^^xsd:integer ;
