concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-794b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "794B Liability of the Commonwealth for certain offences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-794b ;
    values:originalText "(1) Part 2.5 of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the Commonwealth, for the purposes of an offence against: (a) subsection 327A(1) (offence for failing to pay amounts as required) of this Act; or (b) a related offence provision, to the extent that the related offence provision relates to an offence against subsection 327A(1) of this Act; in the same way as that Part applies in relation to a body corporate. (2) It so applies: (a) as if sections 12.4 and 12.5 of the Criminal Code were omitted; and (b) with the following modifications: (i) the modifications set out in the following table (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (ii) such other modifications as are made necessary by the fact that criminal liability is being imposed on a body politic rather than a body corporate (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (iii) any modifications prescribed by the regulations.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Part 2.5 of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the Commonwealth, for the purposes of an offence against: (a) subsection 327A(1) (offence for failing to pay amounts as required) of this Act; or (b) a related offence provision, to the extent that the related offence provision relates to an offence against subsection 327A(1) of this Act; in the same way as that Part applies in relation to a body corporate. (2) It so applies: (a) as if sections 12.4 and 12.5 of the Criminal Code were omitted; and (b) with the following modifications: (i) the modifications set out in the following table (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (ii) such other modifications as are made necessary by the fact that criminal liability is being imposed on a body politic rather than a body corporate (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (iii) any modifications prescribed by the regulations.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b14fdb17ac48ff45ea79d2beca506488414be2c6e8fe6903bd2feda429fd0c6c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "451"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-794b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-794b-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <fair-work-act-2009.pdf> ;
    dc:source "fair-work-act-2009.pdf, p.451" .
doc:sec-794b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "794B Liability of the Commonwealth for certain offences" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Part 2.5 of the Criminal Code applies in relation to the Commonwealth, for the purposes of an offence against: (a) subsection 327A(1) (offence for failing to pay amounts as required) of this Act; or (b) a related offence provision, to the extent that the related offence provision relates to an offence against subsection 327A(1) of this Act; in the same way as that Part applies in relation to a body corporate. (2) It so applies: (a) as if sections 12.4 and 12.5 of the Criminal Code were omitted; and (b) with the following modifications: (i) the modifications set out in the following table (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (ii) such other modifications as are made necessary by the fact that criminal liability is being imposed on a body politic rather than a body corporate (subject to subparagraph (iii)); (iii) any modifications prescribed by the regulations.  Chapter 6  Miscellaneous" ;
