concept:fair-work-act-2009-sec-799 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "799 Regulations dealing with infringement notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-799 ;
    values:originalText "Infringement notices for offences (1) The regulations may provide for a person who is alleged to have committed an offence against the regulations to pay a penalty to the Commonwealth as an alternative to prosecution. (2) The penalty must not exceed one-fifth of the maximum penalty prescribed by the regulations for that offence." ;
    skos:definition "Infringement notices for offences (1) The regulations may provide for a person who is alleged to have committed an offence against the regulations to pay a penalty to the Commonwealth as an alternative to prosecution. (2) The penalty must not exceed one-fifth of the maximum penalty prescribed by the regulations for that offence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f62cef4a1e23031380aabee7d166a90f58ea875d6816bc75b8702aa8a5065084" ;
    cof:pageNumber "458"^^xsd:integer ;
