doc:sec-799 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "799 Regulations dealing with infringement notices" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Infringement notices for offences (1) The regulations may provide for a person who is alleged to have committed an offence against the regulations to pay a penalty to the Commonwealth as an alternative to prosecution. (2) The penalty must not exceed one-fifth of the maximum penalty prescribed by the regulations for that offence." ;
    cof:pageNumber "458"^^xsd:integer .

